cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-flowref: a control-flow-aware cross-reference finder over machine code"
abstract: >
  A data source gets facts out of something that was not built to be queried, and a
  stripped binary is the hardest case of that. This is a control-flow-aware
  cross-reference finder over machine-code disassembly, in Lean 4, so the xrefs it
  reports are claims the language can state properties about rather than output to
  be eyeballed.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fire/datasource-flowref"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - reverse-engineering
  - control-flow-analysis
  - disassembly
references:

